course: dictionary
lesson: 2203
title: Counting down
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A countdown is counting backwards to zero, usually before something starts. Before a rocket launch you hear «10, 9, 8 ... 1, lift-off!» Each number is smaller than the one before, and the count ends at zero.
explain: A countdown can also mean the time just before an important event. «There is a countdown to my birthday: only twelve days to go.» The words countdown to tell you what the time is leading up to, and the number of days shows how close it is.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In «Countdown timers on offers are there to rush you», the timer is a countdown, and the word rush tells you it is meant to make you hurry. Ask yourself: is the number going down or going up? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
fact: A countdown counts backwards, like 3, 2, 1.
fact: Rockets often launch at the end of a countdown, when the count reaches zero.
fact: A countdown can be the time before a birthday, a holiday or New Year.
fact: «Countdown timers on offers» are clocks that make a deal seem to run out soon, so you feel you must hurry.
fact: Real bargains rarely vanish in minutes, so a timer that says hurry is a clue to slow down and think.
exercise: «The countdown reached zero, and the rocket lifted off.» What is a countdown? | A loud noise at night | Counting up to a big number | *Counting backwards to zero | A type of rocket
exercise: «Countdown timers on offers are there to rush you, so you buy before you think.» Why are countdown timers used on offers? | To show that the shop is closed | To count the days until Christmas | *To make you rush and buy before you think | To help you save money slowly
exercise: Maya says, «There is a countdown to my birthday: twelve days to go.» What does the countdown show? | *How much time is left before her birthday | How old Maya is now | How many presents she has | Which day of the week it is
test: Which of these is a countdown? | Counting 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 with no end | Singing a song from start to finish | *Counting 5, 4, 3, 2, 1 before a race starts | Reading a book in silence
test: What does the countdown in «a countdown clock on a special offer» show? | The price of the offer in pounds | *The time left before the offer seems to end | The name of the shop | How many people bought it
exam: Jayden says a countdown must always go up to a big number. Is he right? | *No, a countdown counts backwards to zero | Yes, it always counts up to 100 | Yes, but only on birthdays | No, because countdowns never have numbers
